# Domain Layer Is the Core

- All business rules live in the Domain layer
- Domain imports nothing from frameworks, ORMs, HTTP libraries, or any external dependency
- Entities, Aggregates, and Value Objects are rich objects with behavior — not anemic data structures
- Each Aggregate has a root (Aggregate Root) that controls the lifecycle of the whole
- Value Objects are immutable and self-validate on creation; invalid values fail at construction time

## Anti-Patterns to Avoid

- Putting business logic in controllers, handlers, or repositories
- Leaking persistence concerns (ORM annotations, SQL) into entities
- Mutable Value Objects or entities without invariant enforcement
